  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>1,1-dichloroethane</p><p>Ethylidene chloride is a geminal dihalide with two carbon atoms. In common name system, gem-dihalides are named&nbsp;as alkylidene halides and vic-dihalides are named as alkylene dihalides. The structure of&nbsp;ethylidene chloride is:&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#8722;</mo><msub><mi>CHCl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>.</mo></math></p>"
